      {
        "text": "Name: Candi's mother, surprise guest, tribute to Kato\nType: Character\nDescription: An older, elegant woman who bears a striking resemblance to Candi, likely in her late 40s or 50s. She carries herself with the same practiced, theatrical femininity as her daughter, but with an undercurrent of worldly confidence and authority that comes from age and experience. Her attire is impeccable, perhaps a sophisticated dress in a deep jewel tone, and she is adorned with subtle but high-quality jewelry. She is the surprise guest at the party, brought as a living tribute to Kato.\nBackground: She is the matriarch of a family that has long understood and embraced the dynamics of power and submission. She was the one who first guided Candi, recognizing her daughter's true nature and nurturing it rather than suppressing it. Seeing the profound and positive impact Kato's world has had on her daughter, she sought him out to pay her respects. Her presence at the party is not merely as a guest, but as a deliberate offering from her family line—a testament to their gratitude and a symbolic gesture of fealty. She represents the generational acceptance and celebration of this \"natural order.\"\nSpecial Traits: She possesses a serene and unshakeable poise, completely at ease amidst the raw power of the convention hall. Her voice, when she speaks, is melodious and commanding, capable of silencing a room with a soft-spoken word. She has a deep, intuitive understanding of hierarchy and shows deference to Kato and the Kings not as a submissive, but as an equal peer acknowledging a superior structure. As a tribute, she offers herself and her story as a symbol of devotion, embodying the idea that this philosophy is not a fleeting fantasy but a deep, inherited truth.",
